  "description": "IceCube\u2011Gen2 (also known as IceCube Generation\u202f2 or IC\u2011Gen2) is a large\u2011scale neutrino detection experiment located at the IceCube facility. It is run by the Institute for Cosmic Neutrinos (affiliation record\u202fID\u202f12345) under the Neutrino Observation Collaboration (alternative names: NOCO, Neutrino\u202fObs\u202fCollab). The project was first proposed on\u202f2021\u201107\u201120, received formal approval on\u202f2023\u201105\u201110, began operations on\u202f2022\u201102\u201101 and is scheduled for completion by\u202f2025\u201112\u201131. Its description reads: \u201cA large\u2011scale neutrino detection experiment located at the IceCube facility.\u201d The experiment currently has no dedicated accelerator (accelerator requirement: *We need one*). For correspondence, please contact\u202fcontact@icn.edu, and further information can be found at https://icecube.wisc.edu/gen2. The work is indexed under the field codes \u201cusual\u201d and \u201carXiv\u201d, and is tagged with the free keywords neutrinos, ice, detector, and astrophysics.\n\nAll relationships to other experiments have been curated (curated_relation: true). IceCube\u2011Gen2 lists IceCube (record\u202fID\u202f6789) as its predecessor, a curated relation. The spokesperson team includes Dr. Alice\u202fSmith (record\u202fID\u202f23456), who has been the current spokesperson since\u202f2022\u201101\u201101, and Dr. Bob\u202fJohnson (record\u202fID\u202f34567), who served from\u202f2018\u201106\u201115 until\u202f2021\u201112\u201131; both relations are not curated. Internally, the hidden note records \u201cInternal budget details.\u201d A non\u2011public note indicates \u201cPending approval for extended funding.\u201d Publicly, the experiment promises \u201cPublicly accessible data after 12\u202fmonths.\u201d"
